From 148b20d38ad918954a3bbe8e9d35fda40c347d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:32:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] B5 v3 step 1: the diagnosis of v2's common-epoch alarms
 and the v3 readings (X1 to X11), before any v3 rule code, oracle or data

The diagnosis (b5v3_diagnosis_of_v2_common_epochs, ignored; output xval/area-trust/v3_diagnosis.json.gz) finds each of
the 314 common position-alarm epochs of v2's T4 explained by one satellite: G11 and G14 through broadcast records
marked unhealthy (the engine ignored sv_health), and G03 through a record used two hours before its Toe across a
six-hour gap in the merged file. The 7 loss-of-lock alerts are fewer satellites in view at all four stations at once.
The readings fix the health finding (X2), keep the nearest-Toe selection (X3), fix the SATELLITE_FAULT test (X4),
the loss-of-lock change (X5) and the v3 T1 to T5 (X6 to X11).
